<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lekë Dukagjini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1410–1481</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lekë Dukagjini was an Albanian nobleman of the Dukagjini family, which ruled lands in northern Albania. A contemporary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>, though he also quarrelled with Skanderbeg, and continued the resistance after Skanderbeg's death in 1468. Tradition attributes to him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanun">Kanun</a> of Lekë Dukagjini, the customary law of the northern Albanian highlands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leke-dukagjini.jpg" alt="Lekë Dukagjini" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Postcard image produced by Studio Marubbi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lek%C3%AB_Dukagjini_(portret).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
